# =============================================================================
#  What git should NOT keep
# =============================================================================
#  Everything here is produced by Vivado from files that ARE kept. Committing it
#  would add 76 MB of noise that changes on every build and tells you nothing.
#
#  This list is deliberately the same as the one tools/backup.ps1 excludes. One
#  rule, two implementations - if you change one, change the other.
#
#  Checked before excluding, because leaving out a real source would give you a
#  repository that cannot be built:
#    * system.bd carries all 303 processor parameters itself - the HP ports,
#      their 64-bit widths, the clocks. It is the source.
#    * The project file lists only two block-design files: system.bd and
#      hdl/system_wrapper.v. Both are kept.
#    * build_project.tcl regenerates the rest if it is missing, so a fresh
#      clone simply builds.
# =============================================================================

# --- Vivado's build output: 36 MB, rebuilt every time ------------------------
.cache/
build/
Test_Project.runs/
Test_Project.cache/
Test_Project.hbs/
Test_Project.hw/
Test_Project.sim/
Test_Project.ip_user_files/
*.jou
*.log
*.str
.Xil/
**/.Xil/

# --- Block design output products: 34 MB, generated from system.bd -----------
Test_Project.srcs/sources_1/bd/system/ip/
Test_Project.srcs/sources_1/bd/system/ipshared/

# --- Test output: evidence, not source ---------------------------------------
#  Logs and plots from running the notebooks. Keep the ones that matter by
#  quoting them in CHANGELOG.md, which is where the reasoning lives anyway.
results/

# --- Bitstreams: binary, 2 MB each, and regenerable --------------------------
#  Deliberately NOT in git. A 2 MB binary that changes completely on every build
#  makes the repository grow without limit and cannot be diffed, so it earns
#  nothing. The zip from tools/backup.ps1 keeps the built bitstream; git keeps
#  the source that produces it, and register 0x48 ties the two together.
*.bit
*.bin
*.bif

# --- Python and editor scratch -----------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.ipynb_checkpoints/
tests/python/figs/
bench_coil_results.json
bench_coil_report.md.tmp
bench_coil_results.json.tmp
bench_coil_traces.npz.tmp.npz
pytest-cache-files-*/
pytest-followup-validation/
pytest-temp/
.codex-test-temp/
*~
*.swp
.vscode/
.idea/

# --- Things that should never be committed anywhere --------------------------
*.pem
*.key
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*
